# The deploy is the page plus the JSON it fetches. Everything that builds that
# JSON stays on a laptop.
#
# gemini_server.py and requirements.txt are the two lines that matter: a .py
# at the root with a Handler in it is what made Vercel guess this was a Python
# app and refuse to build. api/analyze.js is the deployed endpoint; the Python
# one is the local dev server and has no business in the bundle.
gemini_server.py
requirements.txt
config.py
pipeline/
twitter-firehose/
__pycache__/
.dev/
.backup/
.vscode/

# Root assets the page does not use -- the font it does use is inlined as
# base64 in dashboard/index.html, so the page is genuinely one file.
*.png
*.ttf
README.md
CLAUDE.md
